;; every corpus the Scheme levels are checked over, each with its pin. Nothing of them is in the tree: a
;; corpus is fetched by `bin/repr-scheme corpus fetch` into :fetched-into (each file from :url-prefix + its
;; path, checked against its SHA-256 here), or read in place (go-whim's whimsical, from a go-whim checkout at
;; its commit and tree hash). Read with the Clojure reader. Keys: :id; :what; :repo, :commit (the revision);
;; :files (path under the corpus -> SHA-256 of the bytes), :count, :bytes (as of SM1); :license (SPDX, or
;; the corpus' own as data), :license-file (the repository's license text, fetched and pinned like a file),
;; :license-note (what was verified); :standard (the report the files are written to, which decides how
;; Chez, the reference, reads them: R6RS mode, SPEC §9); :until (the milestone that first reads it).
;; Licenses are kept here and not in LICENSE.md because nothing of a corpus is distributed (the files are read
;; in place; C's corpora, test/c/corpora.edn, are the precedent).
